# Line endings are pinned so a checkout is byte-identical to the built package
# on every platform. Without this, Git for Windows (core.autocrlf=true by
# default) rewrote text files to CRLF on clone, their SHA-256 no longer matched
# MANIFEST.json, and verify_package.py told a teammate with a perfectly good
# copy to "re-download the package".
* text=auto eol=lf
# The package writes its Windows launchers with CRLF, so check them out that way.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Model checkpoints live in Git LFS (the largest is 107 MB; GitHub's limit is 100 MB).
*.pth filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
